# Line endings are decided here, not by whatever `core.autocrlf` each of us
# happens to have set.
#
# The symptom that earned this file: `make seed` on Windows rewrote all
# thirteen `data/*.json` through `Path.write_text`, which translates "\n" to
# `os.linesep`. On a clone whose git was not normalising, every one of them
# then showed as modified in `git status` with an empty `git diff` -- so
# anybody looking for a real seed-data change had to first prove that thirteen
# files of noise were noise. That matters more here than in most repositories:
# `data/` is the shelf both panels are claimed to have shopped, and
# `predictions/` is evidence. "Modified, but only whitespace" is not a state
# either of those should ever be in.
#
# `scripts/make_seed_data.py` now writes LF itself, which fixes the generator.
# This fixes it for every file, every editor and every clone.
#
# Adding this changed nothing that was already committed: every tracked text
# file in the index was verified LF first, so no file starts showing as
# modified because of it.

# Detect text, store it LF, and check it out LF. A generated file and the
# committed one are then byte-for-byte equal on all three platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the files that carry the contract, the seed data, the
# evidence and the code, so none of them can be reinterpreted by an editor
# setting or a stray tool.
*.json     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.ts       text eol=lf
*.tsx      text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.ini      text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.mermaid  text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf

# The one exception, and the reason `* text=auto eol=lf` is not enough on its
# own: cmd.exe is the only interpreter in this repository that cares. Batch
# files get CRLF in the working tree; git still stores them LF.
*.bat      text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never converted, never diffed as text. `data/models/WaterBottle.glb`
# is the only one of these that is actually committed -- it is the Khronos CC0
# sample model, and its own directory records the hash it must keep -- but the
# generated textures under `web/public/textures/` and the vision clips under
# `data/vision/` are `.gitignore`d rather than impossible, so they are listed
# too in case one is ever committed deliberately.
*.glb      binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.mp4      binary
*.db       binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
